A||N||5||FieroSTETZ||Stolen Fiero returned!||||4||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||02-20-2000||08:44 PM||||i got my fiero back! thats the end of the good news. it was recovered at a rice-boy dragstrip. it was a friend of mine on the force so he gave me a call rather than having it towed. its in my driveway now. whoever took it overheated it, because the coolant level was about 5 oz. my front fascia is cracked really bad, my front 6 month old paint is flaking, it was outta gas (haha for them) the interior is filthy, and my mirrors are almost broken off, not to mention a broken switchplate for the power trunk realease. i dont know what they did to it, but after flushing/refilling the coolant, it keeps overheating and i get a code 32 or 34 (the EGR one) anyone know anything about this? well, i am either gonna sell the fiero or pour all the money from my new job into it... i dont have much, but i think i can make it driveable. also, the little metal things above the side windows, what are they called? when i got the car back they were bent and twisted all to heck||||reg||4
Z||000001||Greg Piet||02-20-2000||09:18 PM||||Well from my understanding an egr code means you have a vaccum leak either at a hose or the egr valve.  That or your EGR solenoid is shot.  I got a solenoid out of an 86 camaro with a 2.8 in it from a junkyard for 5 bucks.   I guess you could always have a melted wire as well.   Good luck, and I hope you get the overheating thing fixed!||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||02-20-2000||09:27 PM||||Make sure you're burping all the air out of the system. Fieros are a pain in the hinny in this regard. If it's still overheating, then you might have a cracked head or blown head gasket. Your insurance company may still "total" it out, if so, you usually have the option to buy it back from them at a very reasonable cost, usually at salvage price. They ought to hang car thieves!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||02-20-2000||11:49 PM||||Good point about buying it back for the salvage price.  My sister just totaled her '90 Pontiac 6000 a few weeks ago.  I'm trying to negotiate a better price for her car because it has Iron Duke.  49k miles and the motor wasn't touched.  So far I've got them down to $500 plus the towing and storage bills.  I can't afford that, but I hope to get them down quite a bit farther.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||02-21-2000||02:51 PM||||I think FieroSTETZ mentioned in an earlier post that he has liability only.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Like batboy said, make sure you have all the air out. <P>How quickly is it overheating? Is it blowing coolant out? How is it running before it overheats?<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Deer_Slayer||02-22-2000||02:36 PM||||Sounds like the rice boys kidnapped it and really tortured it.  Where is this world heading?  ||||reg||13
